## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical CGO memory management and cross-language error handling, plus safe concurrency patterns.

## Key Concepts

- **CGO memory ownership**: Understanding who allocates and frees memory across the C/Go boundary
- **C string to Go string conversion**: Safely converting C strings to Go strings without dangling pointers
- **Error code mapping**: Translating C error codes to idiomatic Go errors
- **Concurrent CGO calls**: Properly handling CGO calls from goroutines

## Code Example

